## Makefile tips and tricks


### $(file) and calculating output directories
```
# top.mk

include nothing.mk
SOURCE_BASE=/home/tnmurphy/src
THIS_MAKEFILE:=$(firstword $(MAKEFILE_LIST))
$(info try writing to a file for $(THIS_MAKEFILE))
BUILD_OUTPUT:=/somewhere
OUTPUT_DIR:=$(BUILD_OUTPUT)/$(patsubst $(SOURCE_BASE)/%,%,$(PWD))
OBJS := a.obj b.obj c.obj
ABS_OBJS:=$(addprefix $(OUTPUT_DIR)/,$(OBJS))
$(file > linker_objs,$(ABS_OBJS))


target:
	$(MAKE) -C sub

```

In a subdirectory: 


```
# sub/Makefile
THIS_MAKEFILE:=$(firstword $(MAKEFILE_LIST))
$(info submakefile $(THIS_MAKEFILE))
```

The output shows that the toplevel makefile and submakefiles can determine their own names.

It shows how to choose an output directory based on the path relative to a source directory
